From 1e28a67f49fc7a701220cceaf84a18d59633547d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:10:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Games: Add RetroAchievements hardcore mode, hidden until
 approved

RetroAchievements award double points for playing without rewind,
loading save states, slow motion and cheats, and decide which clients
may earn those unlocks. This adds the setting, hands it to the game
client and enforces it. The setting stays hidden until RetroAchievements
have approved Kodi. Nothing behind it takes effect while it is off, so
offering it is then a matter of showing the setting.

While hardcore is on, loading a save state, rewind, seeking backwards,
slow motion and cheats are refused, each with a notification. Saving a
state, pausing and fast forward stay available. Resuming from a save
state drops back to casual. A rewind or slow motion already running
when hardcore starts returns to normal speed, and if the emulator
refuses hardcore, Kodi turns the setting off and says so.

The achievements window gains a hardcore toggle beside encore, which
asks first during a game because turning it on restarts the game. The
game-start notification leads with the mode, and
RetroPlayer.AchievementsHardcore lets a skin show it.

A change to the setting holds its lock while observers run, and the
client's observer takes the client lock, so the mode is cached apart
from the setting for readers that hold the client lock.
